# Binaries and build output. Build outside the repo (`go build -o ../bin/...`) so a stray
# executable cannot be committed by accident.
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.test
*.out
bin/

# Load-test credentials, kept out of git on purpose: this file holds live bearer tokens and API
# keys for the seeder's tenants. It is regenerated by the seed command and expires with the token
# TTL, so it has no business in history.
load/sessions.json
load/creds.json

# Run artifacts are NOT ignored here. `load/results.json` is the record behind every number quoted
# in the README, and an artifact that cannot be committed cannot be checked — the same reasoning the
# sibling repository records for its own results file.

# Secrets. `.env.example` carries placeholders and is committed; a real `.env` never is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local data volumes, if anyone points compose at a bind mount.
data/

# Logs (the migration and smoke-test logs are run artifacts, not sources).
*.log

# Coverage output.
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
